  "checked": "2026-10-07",
  "notes": "Guests span 3 category pages the site itself calls out in its guest nav (Entertainment Guests, Artists and Creators, Cosplay Guests): 2 cancelled 'NO LONGER APPEARING' entertainment guests (Lamorne Morris, Tony Hale) were skipped per the schema rule. The Artists and Creators page (152 photo candidates) mixes two different lists on one page: the first 39 (Scott Snyder through Brett Bean) are sorted newest-announced-first exactly like the other guest categories and are individually-sourced industry names with their own photos, so they're included as 'comics' guests -- their cards show name + appearance days only, no credit text, so Known for is left blank rather than filled from outside knowledge. From entry 41 onward ('1First Comics Presents: Jared Sams' through 'Verbal Ase', then a cancelled 'Tom King') the list switches to strict alphabetical-by-name order, every photo's filename is literally the shared template 'LA Comic Con Artist Alley Guest Headshot', and bios are generic role tags (Artist/Writer/Inker/Penciler/Colorist) with no specific credited work -- this is the con's Artist Alley directory surfaced on the same page/template, which the research rules say to skip, so those ~110 names were not picked. Known-for text for the Entertainment Guests and Critical Role/game-VA block was trimmed from longer on-card credit lists (e.g. Critical Role credits for O'Brien/Riegel/Jaffe/Moore/Carazo/Ward were identical on-card ('Critical Role') so all six are filed as voice for consistency). Cosplay guest cards only say 'Cosplayer' or 'Group' with no other text, used verbatim (as 'Cosplay group' for the three team entries). No organizer name is printed anywhere on the rendered homepage, so organizer is left blank rather than guessed. Refute pass (2026-10-05): a scan flagged some photos as looking older than this edition, but a fresh re-extraction of all three guest pages shows every picked guest's image carries a Squarespace upload timestamp between 2026-07-03 and 2026-10-02 -- months after LACC's actual previous edition (Sept 26-28, 2025, confirmed by search) and squarely in this 2026 edition's own run-up, with no 2025-dated images found -- so the lineup is upheld as current. 2026-10-07 refresh: unchanged; the only new card on the Artists and Creators page (Deegan Puchkors) sits in the Artist Alley directory block (after the alphabetical list, a generic headshot with no credit), which is skipped per the rule above, and no picked guest was missing."
